# Store LF in the repository and check out LF: this project requires LF everywhere, on every
# platform.  A CRLF file on a Windows checkout is a defect, not a preference.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.c    text eol=lf
*.h    text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.exe  binary
*.o    binary
# Captured output under doc/measurements/ is EVIDENCE, not source, and some records legitimately
# contain CRLF or bare CR bytes from the console they were captured on.  `-text` means "never
# convert", so the bytes in the repository are the bytes that were observed, on every platform -
# and a fresh clone no longer reports a dozen records as modified merely because a checkout would
# have rewritten their line endings (which is exactly how a Linux clone looked dirty after a
# hard reset, and what made the state of that machine read as untrustworthy).
doc/measurements/** -text
